---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About Us | UK Mountains Directory"
  description="Learn about UK Mountains Directory and our mission to provide comprehensive information about mountains across the United Kingdom."
>
  <div class="about-page">
    <div class="about-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <h1>About UK Mountains Directory</h1>
        <p class="hero-text">
          Your comprehensive guide to exploring the mountains of the United Kingdom
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="container">
      <div class="about-content">
        <section class="content-section">
          <h2>Our Mission</h2>
          <p>
            UK Mountains Directory is dedicated to providing accurate, comprehensive, and accessible information about
            every significant peak across England, Scotland, and Wales. Whether you're an experienced mountaineer
            planning your next Munro, a casual hiker looking for weekend adventures, or simply curious about the
            magnificent peaks that define our landscape, we're here to help.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="content-section">
          <h2>What We Offer</h2>
          <div class="features-grid">
            <div class="feature-card">
              <div class="feature-icon">⛰️</div>
              <h3>Comprehensive Database</h3>
              <p>
                Detailed information on Munros, Corbetts, Marilyns, and other significant peaks across the UK,
                including heights, locations, and classifications.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="feature-card">
              <div class="feature-icon">📍</div>
              <h3>Location Services</h3>
              <p>
                Find mountains near you with our geolocation feature, complete with distances and directions to
                help plan your next adventure.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="feature-card">
              <div class="feature-icon">🔍</div>
              <h3>Smart Search</h3>
              <p>
                Powerful search and filtering tools to help you find the perfect mountain based on region, height,
                classification, and more.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="feature-card">
              <div class="feature-icon">📚</div>
              <h3>Rich Information</h3>
              <p>
                Discover the history, interesting facts, nearby facilities, and local attractions for each mountain
                to enhance your experience.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="content-section">
          <h2>Mountain Classifications</h2>
          <div class="classifications">
            <div class="classification-item">
              <h3>Munros</h3>
              <p>
                Scottish mountains over 3,000 feet (914.4 meters). Named after Sir Hugh Munro, who first cataloged
                them in 1891. There are 282 Munros in Scotland.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="classification-item">
              <h3>Corbetts</h3>
              <p>
                Scottish mountains between 2,500 and 3,000 feet (762-914 meters) with a drop of at least 500 feet
                on all sides. Named after John Rooke Corbett.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="classification-item">
              <h3>Marilyns</h3>
              <p>
                Mountains in the British Isles with a prominence of at least 150 meters (492 feet). The name is a
                pun on Munro, with the M representing "minimum" prominence.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="content-section">
          <h2>Safety First</h2>
          <p>
            We believe that informed adventurers are safe adventurers. While we provide comprehensive information
            about each mountain, we always emphasize the importance of proper preparation, appropriate equipment,
            and respect for the natural environment.
          </p>
          <div class="safety-tips">
            <ul>
              <li>Always check weather forecasts before setting out</li>
              <li>Inform someone of your planned route and expected return time</li>
              <li>Carry appropriate equipment including maps, compass, and first aid kit</li>
              <li>Know your limits and choose routes appropriate for your fitness level</li>
              <li>Respect local guidelines and access restrictions</li>
              <li>Leave no trace - take your litter home</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="content-section">
          <h2>Our Commitment</h2>
          <p>
            We are committed to maintaining accurate and up-to-date information about UK mountains. Our database
            is regularly updated to reflect changes in access, facilities, and other relevant information. If you
            notice any inaccuracies or have suggestions for improvements, please <a href="/contact">contact us</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="content-section cta-section">
          <h2>Start Exploring</h2>
          <p>
            Ready to discover the mountains of the UK? Start your journey today and find your next adventure.
          </p>
          <a href="/" class="btn btn-primary">Explore Mountains</a>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about-page {
    background: var(--color-neutral-50);
  }

  .about-hero {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0f766e 0%, #14b8a6 100%);
    padding: var(--spacing-3xl) 0;
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-3xl);
  }

  .about-hero h1 {
    color: white;
    font-size: 3rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
  }

  .hero-text {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .about-content {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding-bottom: var(--spacing-3xl);
  }

  .content-section {
    background: white;
    padding: var(--spacing-xl);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);
  }

  .content-section h2 {
    color: var(--color-neutral-900);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
  }

  .content-section p {
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--color-neutral-700);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
  }

  .features-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--spacing-lg);
    margin-top: var(--spacing-lg);
  }

  .feature-card {
    padding: var(--spacing-lg);
    background: var(--color-neutral-50);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .feature-icon {
    font-size: 3rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
  }

  .feature-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    color: var(--color-neutral-900);
  }

  .feature-card p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-neutral-600);
  }

  .classifications {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--spacing-lg);
    margin-top: var(--spacing-lg);
  }

  .classification-item {
    padding: var(--spacing-lg);
    background: var(--color-neutral-50);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-primary);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  }

  .classification-item h3 {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
  }

  .classification-item p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-neutral-700);
  }

  .safety-tips {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #fef3c7 0%, #fde68a 100%);
    padding: var(--spacing-lg);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    border: 2px solid #f59e0b;
    margin-top: var(--spacing-lg);
  }

  .safety-tips ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: var(--spacing-xl);
  }

  .safety-tips li {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    color: var(--color-neutral-800);
  }

  .cta-section {
    text-align: center;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0f766e 0%, #14b8a6 100%);
  }

  .cta-section h2 {
    color: white;
  }

  .cta-section p {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
  }

  .cta-section .btn {
    background: white;
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }

  .cta-section .btn:hover {
    background: var(--color-neutral-100);
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .about-hero h1 {
      font-size: 2rem;
    }

    .hero-text {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }

    .content-section h2 {
      font-size: 1.75rem;
    }

    .features-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
